=== SIGNATURE ===
xrank(value, array, [order])

=== COMMENT ===
Like the built-in RANK but works on arrays.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(value, array, [order], LET(
   rank_style_order, IF(ISOMITTED(order), 0, z_scalar(order)),
   sort_style_order, IF(rank_style_order = 0, -1, 1),
   IFNA(XMATCH(z_scalar(value), SORT(TOCOL(array), 1, sort_style_order)), "")
))

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Rank of a value within an array.

Arguments:
  value   - the value to rank.
  array   - the set of values to rank within.
  [order] - 0 = descending (default), 1 = ascending.

Single-value arguments (flags, counts, delimiters, a single lookup value) may arrive as 1x1 arrays (TOCOL(x), {x}, a one-cell FILTER/INDEX result); they are collapsed to true scalars with z_scalar, so they behave exactly like the plain value.

Returns:
  The 1-based rank of value among array, or "" if value is not found in array.

Example:
  xrank(50, scores)
